  "subdivision_of_building": "Ground floor. Retail unit A only.",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "Retail Unit A of Walrond house, currently unoccupied, is proposed for use as a reformer pilates studio. This should not require a change of use as it has existing use class E consent. \nThe client has deemed the existing automatic entrance doors at the Matthias road entrance to be unsuitable for the proposed usage of the space and is so proposing development works to change the existing door to glazed, hinged, double doors. The doors are to be in the same location as the existing with no changes to structural openings. There is also an accessible WC with ventilation panel requirements to the external facades included in the submission. All interior proposals are indicative. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;All new external facing and roofing materials in respect of all the works hereby approved (and any other incidental works carried out in this connection) shall match those of the existing building in respect of materials used, detailed execution and finished appearance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\nREASON: In the interests of the visual amenities of the surrounding area.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
